DATA SCIENCE RESEARCH CAPSTONE
RESULTS SUMMARY

Project Title:
Predicting Student Academic Performance Using Machine Learning

MODEL USED
Random Forest Regression

INPUT FEATURES
1. Study Hours
2. Attendance
3. Previous Score
4. Assignments Completed
5. Sleep Hours

TARGET VARIABLE
Final Score

EVALUATION METRICS
1. Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
2. Mean Squared Error (MSE)
3. Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
4. R2 Score

RESULT ANALYSIS
The machine learning model is trained to predict student final academic
scores using study habits, attendance, previous academic performance,
assignment completion and sleep hours.

The model performance can be evaluated using MAE, MSE, RMSE and R2 Score.

FEATURE IMPORTANCE
The Random Forest model calculates the importance of each input feature.
This helps identify which factors contribute more to predicting academic
performance.

CONCLUSION
The project demonstrates an end-to-end data science workflow for predicting
student academic performance using machine learning.

The system can be useful for academic monitoring, student progress
analysis and data-driven educational planning.

NOTE
The dataset used in this capstone project is a demonstration dataset.
Further validation with larger real-world educational datasets is required.
